## Define what is meant by the term "artificial intelligence".

Artificial intelligence (often abbreviated AI) refers to the development of computer systems that are able to perform tasks that would typically require human intelligence. These tasks can include activities such as understanding natural language, recognizing images, playing games, and solving problems. At its core, artificial intelligence involves the creation of intelligent machines that can learn, reason, perceive, and react to their environment in ways that were previously thought to be exclusive to humans. AI technology can range from basic programs that can carry out simple automated tasks, to complex systems that can learn and adapt to new information to become increasingly sophisticated in their abilities.

